  "complete": "All five series are fully listed: 144 of 144 cards, each checked against two independent collector lists and against photos of the real card backs. Not listed as separate entries: foil versions of the regular cards and reprints of older cards in later series, which carry the same number but a newer card design.",
  "rarity_notes": "Regular cards print one rarity on the back: COMMON, RARE or UNIQUE, and the single Series 5 card says LEGENDARY. Raw Thrills publishes only one set of odds: a one-in-ten chance of a Hero card on every start (Arcade Heroes, Series 3 launch). The machine gives out one card per play. There are no published odds for Common, Rare or Unique, and one collector site says they do not seem to come out any less often. Raw Thrills calls Chicken Jockey its first Legendary card, but it has not said how many were printed or what the odds are. Numbers are shown as printed without the leading '#': Series 1 uses two digits (#04/60), later regular cards print #N/total-at-that-time, and Hero cards print '#N of total'.",
  "not_listed": "Foil versions of the regular cards (every card has one, but no full list was found) and reprints of older cards in later series (same number, newer design) are not separate entries. A foil or a reprint counts as the same card here."
 },
